# Documentation (Cursor)

## Build

```bash
py -3.12 -m mkdocs serve
```

Navigation is defined in `mkdocs.yml`. Add new pages to the `nav` tree.

## Style

Follow `.claude/rules/docs-style.md`: sentence case headings, no em dashes or semicolons, concise technical prose, physics-first where relevant. Key rules:

- No AI buzzwords (leverage, utilize, delve, seamlessly, etc.)
- Short paragraphs (3-4 sentences max)
- Active voice, present tense
- Specific numbers, not vague language
- MathJax for equations: inline `$S_{ab}$`, display `$$...$$`
- Code blocks need language tags (`python`, `bash`, `json`)
- Use `-` for all bullets (not `*`)

Internal design notes under `docs/internal/` are not required to be perfect polish but should stay accurate.
